In article <C5Gnr3.1L9@cg57.uucp> mcohan@cg57.uucp (Max Cohan) writes:
>1) Polypiling items is good, but it should have a greater tendency to produce LESSER items... I think polymorphing items is a big part of the game, it's kinda
>a neat idea... I rarely use it to tell the truth... a good way to fix things
>might be to not allow piling... a few items piled together would 'melt' together either making one item or just a pile of junk or, of course, a golem

Done.  Items tend to disintegrate (shuddering vibrations) when in
large polymorphed piles.  They also make golems.

>4) it'd be nice to have a way for priests to bless items and or make altars

All characters can bless items.  Making altars just anywhere would
make priests too powerful.  They already have two special abilities.

>5) a temple LEVEL would be appropriate

Done.  There are four places in the game guaranteed to have temples,
and one has a temple of each alignment.  Some of the quest levels
(such as caveman and knight) have extra temples.

The game would be a lot easier, though, if there was a temple/altar
around level 10-20 in every game.

>6) a pickup options with Items would be VERY good ie pickup only $/! automatically

Yes.

>7) praying should have a few options... ie 1) just pray - tells you status with god 2) pray for help - like pray is now 3) pray for items - this is if you're VERY lucky, and in VERY good with your god...you can ask him/her to give you something

Cut down your line length.  You can get your god's status or ask for
an item by sacrificing a corpse.  Praying always asks for help.

>8) it might be nice to get an 'are you sure(y/n)' message before stepping into water/lava/etc... or maybe that kinda ruins the point? :)

This debate has gone on for years.  The dev team _LIKES_ drowning
players like this.  You now have a chance of climbing out.

Actually on long moves (shift key and direction), it would be good if
you stopped before blundering into traps and water/lava, or even
boulders.  Lots of other things make you stop.

>9) as soon as you pick up the bell/book/etc it should be 'stuck' to you so
> if you leave the level without it...it will somehow appear again... IE
>a monster on the level will have it, etc... 
>in the case of the amulet it might be good to have the wizard always appear
>so if you do something stupid like kill him where you can't get the item,
>he would reappear on the next level WITH that item... it would solve alot of progoblems...

Why?  It's not supposed to be easy.  The special artifacts should be
non-destroyable, though.  At least the Book of the Dead is fireproof.

>11) a new extended command #beg - for forgivness... you would be able to use it in case you attack something peacefull by accident (ie throwing something)

Why?  The gods are selfish.  They'll only forgive you if you do
something for them....

>
>12) #chat should work across the room, not just next to you, maybe for 5-10 spaces

Done.  Try it in a shop, standing on an item.

>
>13) special weapons should either auto-identify or have special messages: ie
>like when you pick up a quest item -
>mojo: you feel the power of thor's hammer, etc
>Sting: as you inscribe the magic words in the dagger... etc

Um, the name is already on the weapon.  You see it when you pick it
up.  What more do you want?

>14) Quest items from other classes should either be ALIGNMENT based only or
>not be wishable...makes a character WAY too powerful to have more than ONE quest
>item

Maybe.  You can't get an artifact different than your alignment,
though.

>15) maybe it's time to split things into Races, classes, and alignment
>I hate having to restart all the time to get a lawful character when I want one or a chaotic (or a neutral for that matter) it'd be simpler to have you be able to CHOOSE (within class/race limitations of course) same with PET! you should always get a dog if you want a dog...and vice versa

You can set an option to always ask for a dog (or cat).  Priests are
the only characters with different alignments.  If you want chaotic,
play a barbarian or elf.

>16) pets should be made a little smarter!!!! they should come to you when you 
>are getting attacked....GUARD when you're frozen/paralyzed/etc

Aw, c'mon.  It's a DOG!

>Hunt: goes out and attracts monsters, kills 'em, and brings corpse to you

It always does this, but generally eats the corpse.

>fetch: brings all items it finds to you

Throw a tripe ration at a dog if you want this.  Non-eating monsters
do it anyway.

>17) the uncursed magic whistle should bring pet(s) into room
>    the blessed magic whistle should ALWAYS bring pets next to you

They both always bring the pet next to you.  After that, they may move
away, though.

>18) you should be able to find other backpacks you start out with a medium sized one and can get a larger one, maybe a water proof one, and a backpack of holding

Use bags.  There is a waterproof one and a bag of holding.

>my last request is REALLY non-trivial
>personally I really LIKE one thing about omega
>you can place items exactly where you want them or in your pack
>if something like this could be adapted to nethack
>it would make it %100 the best game around instead of only
>%99 :)

Done.  Use the #adjust command.

